($t$Santalum haleakalae$t$, $t$Santalum haleakalae$t$, $t$Santalaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Santalaceae. Portamento: Tree. Altezza massima indicativa: 3 m. Santalum haleakalae or commonly known as Haleakala Sandalwood or Lilahi is an evergreen flowering shrub or tree growing 2-4 m in height and 20 cm in bole diameter. It has a dense crown. It is hemi-parasitic like other species in the Santalum genus. It is mixed with other plants for medicinal uses particularly in the treatment of venereal diseases, sores, dandruff and head lice. The seed is edible with tasty flavor but not frequently consumed because it is more valued for propagation than as food. The heartwood yields essential oil which is used in perfumery, cosmetics, incense sticks, aromatherapy, and others. The wood is commonly used for carvings, musical instruments, handicrafts, and decorative furniture.$t$, $j${"luce": "Tollera: pieno sole, mezz'ombra", "acqua": "Scarsa, tollera la siccità una volta ambientata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Haleakala Sandalwood, Lliahi$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Santalaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": null, "finestra_semina": [], "finestra_trapianto": [], "resistenza_gelo": "bassa", "spaziatura_cm": null, "consoci